      "term": "Minor drug possession offense"
    },
    {
      "definition": "(4) \"Qualifying assault offense\" means a violation of section 2903.13 of the Revised Code for which the penalty provision in division (C)(8)(b) or (C)(9)(b) of that section applies.\n\n(L) At the time of sentencing an offender for any sexually oriented offense, if the offender is a tier III sex offender/child-victim offender relative to that offense and the offender does not serve a prison term or jail term, the court may require that the offender be monitored by means of a global positioning device. If the court requires such monitoring, the cost of monitoring shall be borne by the offender. If the offender is indigent, the cost of compliance shall be paid by the crime victims reparations fund.\n\nLast updated January 25, 2023 at 10:11 AM",
      "id": "2929.13-qualifying-assault-offense",
      "normalized": "qualifying assault offense",
      "scope": "(K) As used in this section:",
      "section": "2929.13",
      "source_title": "Section 2929.13 - Sanction imposed by degree of felony.",
